oned in Śloka 5, Chapter 35, Ādi Parva of the <a class="pe_a_pada" href="महाभारत">mahābhārata</a>. Arjuna's father-inlaw and Ulūpi's father, <a class="pe_a_pada" href="कौरव्य">kauravya</a> belonged to the family of this serpent. (See Śloka 18, Chapter 213, Ādi Parva).</div></div></div>

