e_a_pada" href="सेवेन् इस्लन्द्स्">seven islands</a> of ancient times. The wind around <a class="pe_a_pada" href="तेन्">ten</a> yojanas of Plakṣa is very fragrant because it carries the divine fragrance being emitted always from the bodies of <a class="pe_a_pada" href="पार्वती">pārvatī</a> and her attendants, who drink water from river <a class="pe_a_pada" href="अरुणोदा">aruṇodā</a>. (<a class="pe_a_pada" href="देवी">devī</a> <a class="pe_a_pada" href="भागवत">bhāgavata</a>, Aṣṭama <a class="pe_a_pada" href="स्कन्ध">skandha</a>).</div></div></div>

