</a>. He got this name because he desisted from doing loathful acts. “I will never resort to loathful deeds in war. Therefore the <a class="pe_a_pada" href="देवस्">devas</a> and men call me Bibhatsu”. (<a class="pe_a_pada" href="महाभारत">mahābhārata</a>, <a class="pe_a_pada" href="विराट">virāṭa</a> Parva, Chapter 44, Stanza 18).</div></div></div>

