 href="मरीचि">marīci</a>, <a class="pe_a_pada" href="अंगिरस्">aṅgiras</a>, <a class="pe_a_pada" href="अत्रि">atri</a>, <a class="pe_a_pada" href="पुलस्त्य">pulastya</a>, <a class="pe_a_pada" href="पुलह">pulaha</a>, Kṛtu and <a class="pe_a_pada" href="वसिष्ठ">vasiṣṭha</a>. These saints are called by the name Citraśikhaṇḍīs also. (Śloka 29, Chapter 336, <a class="pe_a_pada" href="शान्ति">śānti</a> Parva).</div></div></div>

