Parva, Chapter 10, Stanza 29). He sits in the Durbar of <a class="pe_a_pada" href="कुबेर">kubera</a> (God of wealth) and sings. He was the teacher of Rukmin, the son of <a class="pe_a_pada" href="भीष्मक">bhīṣmaka</a> and he gave a bow to his pupil Rukmin. (<a class="pe_a_pada" href="महाभारत">mahābhārata</a>, Udyoga Parva, Chapter 158.)</div></div></div>

