he <a class="pe_a_pada" href="भरद्वाज">bharadvāja</a> family who was also well-versed in Kūṭanīti. He was an adviser to <a class="pe_a_pada" href="शत्रुञ्जय">śatruñjaya</a>, King of <a class="pe_a_pada" href="सौवीर">sauvīra</a>. (Chapter 140, <a class="pe_a_pada" href="शान्ति">śānti</a> Parva).</div></div></div>

