f="इन्दिअ">india</a>. It is stated in <a class="pe_a_pada" href="महाभारत">mahābhārata</a>, Ādi Parva, Chapter 67, Stanza 64 that this King was born from a portion of the <a class="pe_a_pada" href="असुर">asura</a> called <a class="pe_a_pada" href="क्रोधवश">krodhavaśa</a>. The King ruled over the country called Kulūta. In the battle of <a class="pe_a_pada" href="भारत">bhārata</a> he fought on the side of the <a class="pe_a_pada" href="कौरवस्">kauravas</a> and was killed by Bhīmasena. (M.B. <a class="pe_a_pada" href="कर्ण">karṇa</a> Parva, Chapter 12, Stanza 44).</div></div></div>

