_pada" href="प्रत्यूष">pratyūṣa</a> is one of the <a class="pe_a_pada" href="अष्टवसुस्">aṣṭavasus</a>. The <a class="pe_a_pada" href="अष्टवसुस्">aṣṭavasus</a> are <a class="pe_a_pada" href="आप">āpa</a>, <a class="pe_a_pada" href="ध्रुव">dhruva</a>, <a class="pe_a_pada" href="सोम">soma</a>, <a class="pe_a_pada" href="धर्म">dharma</a>, <a class="pe_a_pada" href="अनिल">anila</a>, <a class="pe_a_pada" href="अग्नि">agni</a>, <a class="pe_a_pada" href="प्रत्यूष">pratyūṣa</a> and <a class="pe_a_pada" href="प्रभास">prabhāsa</a>. The sage <a class="pe_a_pada" href="देवल">devala</a> is the son of <a class="pe_a_pada" href="प्रत्यूष">pratyūṣa</a>. (Śloka 17, Chapter 66, Ādi Parva).</div></div></div>

