ि">cedi</a>. He was a friend and supporter of the <a class="pe_a_pada" href="पाण्डवस्">pāṇḍavas</a>. During the <a class="pe_a_pada" href="अश्वमेध">aśvamedha</a> he helped <a class="pe_a_pada" href="अर्जुन">arjuna</a> to lead the yājñic horse. (Aśvamedhika Parva, Chapter 83, Verse 3).</div></div></div>

