/div></div>

सरस्वती_४|सरस्वती|సరస్వతీ_౪|సరస్వతీ|ಸರಸ್ವತೀ_೪|ಸರಸ್ವತೀ|sarasvatī_4|sarasvatī|sarasvatii_4|sarasvatii|sarasvatee_4|sarasvatee|_pe_@6298|_pe_pn696R
<style>div.pe_tera{ font-family:Verdana, "Lucida Sans Unicode", sans-serif; margin: 0 auto 0 auto; line-height:1.5em; color:black; } div.pe_patra{ margin:0 auto 0 auto; padding: 1em; max-width:55.8em; font-size: 1em; } div.pe_vibhaaga_1{ margin-top:0.5em; } p.pe_vibhaaga_2{ margin-left:1em; } div.pe_shiram{ font-stle:bold; min-width:7em; padding:0.3em; font-size:1.5em; border:1px solid black; min-width:7em; } span.pe_pradhaanapada{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold text-decoration:underline; color:black; } span.pe_vibhaaganaama_1{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; color:#133b5a; } span.pe_vibhaagasaMkhya_1{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; color:#133b5a; } a.pe_a_pglink{ text-decoration:none; color:blue; } a.pe_a_pada:link,a.pe_a_pada:visited,a.pe_a_pada{ text-decoration:none; color:#1A163A; } a.pe_a_pada_v:link,a.pe_a_pada_v:visited{ text-decoration:none; color:inherit; } a.pe_a_pada:hover{ text-decoration: underline; color:#1A163A; } a.pe_a_pada_v:hover{ text-decoration: underline; } div.pe_shir_shira{ max-width:15em; text-align:left; float:left; margin:0; }  div.pe_shiraputa{ max-width:15em; text-align:right; float:right; } div.pe_vivarana{ text-align:justify; } blockquote.pe_padyam{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; font-size:1.7em; } table.pe_cnpaTTika{ margin-left:2em; } </style><br><div class="pe_tera"><div class="pe_patra"><div class="pe_shir_shira"><div class="pe_shiram">सरस्वती ४</div></div><div class="pe_shiraputa"><a class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_@6297">«</a>word2<a class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_@6299">»</a><br><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn696L">↶</a><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn696R">P696R</a><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn697L">↷</a></div><div class="floatclr" style="clear:both;"><hr><br></div><div class="pe_vivarana"><span class="pe_pradhaanapada">SARASVATĪ IV</span>  . Wife of Dadhīci maharṣi. The couple had a son called <a class="pe_a_pada" href="सारस्वत">sārasvata</a>. (<a class="pe_a_pada" href="ब्रह्माण्ड">brahmāṇḍa</a> <a class="pe_a_pada" href="पुराण">purāṇa</a>, 101, Verse 9).</div></div></div>

सरस्वतीसागरसंगम|सरस्वतीसागरसङ्गम|సరస్వతీసాగరసంగమ|సరస్వతీసాగరసఙ్గమ|ಸರಸ್ವತೀಸಾಗರಸಂಗಮ|ಸರಸ್ವತೀಸಾಗರಸಙ್ಗಮ|sarasvatīsāgarasaṅgama|sarasvatiisaagarasaMgama|sarasvateesaagarasaMgama|sarasvatiisaagarasangama|sarasvateesaagarasangama|_pe_@6299|_pe_pn696R
<style>div.pe_tera{ font-family:Verdana, "Lucida Sans Unicode", sans-serif; margin: 0 auto 0 auto; line-height:1.5em; color:black; } div.pe_patra{ margin:0 auto 0 auto; padding: 1em; max-width:55.8em; font-size: 1em; } div.pe_vibhaaga_1{ margin-top:0.5em; } p.pe_vibhaaga_2{ margin-left:1em; } div.pe_shiram{ font-stle:bold; min-width:7em; padding:0.3em; font-size:1.5em; border:1px solid black; min-width:7em; } span.pe_pradhaanapada{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold text-decoration:underline; color:black; } span.pe_vibhaaganaama_1{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; color:#133b5a; } span.pe_vibhaagasaMkhya_1{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; color:#133b5a; } a.pe_a_pglink{ text-decoration:none; color:blue; } a.pe_a_pada:link,a.pe_a_pada:visited,a.pe_a_pada{ text-decoration:none; color:#1A163A; } a.pe_a_pada_v:link,a.pe_a_pada_v:visited{ text-decoration:none; color:inherit; } a.pe_a_pada:hover{ text-decoration: underline; color:#1A163A; } a.pe_a_pada_v:hover{ text-decoration: underline; } div.pe_shir_shira{ max-width:15em; text-align:left; float:left; margin:0; }  div.pe_shiraputa{ max-width:15em; text-align:right; float:right; } div.pe_vivarana{ text-align:justify; } blockquote.pe_padyam{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; font-size:1.7em; } table.pe_cnpaTTika{ margin-left:2em; } </style><br><div class="pe_tera"><div class="pe_patra"><div class="pe_shir_shira"><div class="pe_shiram">सरस्वतीसागरसंगम</div></div><div class="pe_shiraputa"><a class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_@6298">«</a>word3<a class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_@6300">»</a><br><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn696L">↶</a><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn696R">P696R</a><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn697L">↷</a></div><div class="floatclr" style="clear:both;"><hr><br></div><div class="pe_vivarana"><span class="pe_pradhaanapada">SARASVATĪSĀGARASAṄGAMA</span>  . The point where <a class="pe_a_pada" href="सरस्वती">sarasvatī</a> joins the ocean. It is considered to be a holy place. <a class="pe_a_pada" href="चन्द्र">candra</a> regained his brilliance once dimmed by the curse of <a class="pe_a_pada" href="दक्ष">dakṣa</a> by bathing at this holy place. (For details see under <a class="pe_a_pada" href="चन्द्र">candra</a> IV, <a class="pe_a_pada" href="पर">para</a> 6).</div></div></div>

सरस्वतीसंगम|सरस्वतीसङ्गम|సరస్వతీసంగమ|సరస్వతీసఙ్గమ|ಸರಸ್ವತೀಸಂಗಮ|ಸರಸ್ವತೀಸಙ್ಗಮ|sarasvatīsaṅgama|sarasvatiisaMgama|sarasvateesaMgama|sarasvatiisangama|sarasvateesangama|_pe_@6300|_pe_pn696R
<style>div.pe_tera{ font-family:Verdana, "Lucida Sans Unicode", sans-serif; margin: 0 auto 0 auto; line-height:1.5em; color:black; } div.pe_patra{ margin:0 auto 0 auto; padding: 1em; max-width:55.8em; font-size: 1em; } div.pe_vibhaaga_1{ margin-top:0.5em; } p.pe_vibhaaga_2{ margin-left:1em; } div.pe_shiram{ font-stle:bold; min-width:7em; padding:0.3em; font-size:1.5em; border:1px solid black; min-width:7em; } span.pe_pradhaanapada{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold text-decoration:underline; color:black; } span.pe_vibhaaganaama_1{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; color:#133b5a; } span.pe_vibhaagasaMkhya_1{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; color:#133b5a; } a.pe_a_pglink{ text-decoration:none; color:blue; } a.pe_a_pada:link,a.pe_a_pada:visited,a.pe_a_pada{ text-decoration:none; color:#1A163A; } a.pe_a_pada_v:link,a.pe_a_pada_v:visited{ text-decoration:none; color:inherit; } a.pe_a_pada:hover{ text-decoration: underline; color:#1A163A; } a.pe_a_pada_v:hover{ text-decoration: underline; } div.pe_shir_shira{ max-width:15em; text-align:left; float:left; margin:0; }  div.pe_shiraputa{ max-width:15em; text-align:right; float:right; } div.pe_vivarana{ text-align:justify; } blockquote.pe_padyam{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; font-size:1.7em; } table.pe_cnpaTTika{ margin-left:2em; } </style><br><div class="pe_tera"><div class="pe_patra"><div class="pe_shir_shira"><div class="pe_shiram">सरस्वतीसंगम</div></div><div class="pe_shiraputa"><a class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_@6299">«</a>word4<a class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_@6301">»</a><br><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn696L">↶</a><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn696R">P696R</a><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn697L">↷</a></div><div class="floatclr" style="clear:both;"><hr><br></div><div class="pe_vivarana"><span class="pe_pradhaanapada">SARASVATĪSAṄGAMA</span>  . A sacred place. <a class="pe_a_pada" href="ब्रह्मा">brahmā</a> and the maharṣis once worshipped <a class="pe_a_pada" href="विष्णु">viṣṇu</a> here. He who bathes here will attain Brahmaloka. (Vana Parva, Chapter 83, Verse 151).</div></div></div>

सरस्वत्यर्णुआसंगम|सरस्वत्यर्णुआसङ्गम|సరస్వత్యర్ణుఆసంగమ|సరస్వత్యర్ణుఆసఙ్గమ|ಸರಸ್ವತ್ಯರ್ಣುಆಸಂಗಮ|ಸರಸ್ವತ್ಯರ್ಣುಆಸಙ್ಗಮ|sarasvatyarṇuāsaṅgama|sarasvatyarNuaasaMgama|sarasvatyarNuaasangama|_pe_@6301|_pe_pn696R
<style>div.pe_tera{ font-family:Verdana, "Lucida Sans Unicode", sans-serif; margin: 0 auto 0 auto; line-height:1.5em; color:black; } div.pe_patra{ margin:0 auto 0 auto; padding: 1em; max-width:55.8em; font-size: 1em; } div.pe_vibhaaga_1{ margin-top:0.5em; } p.pe_vibhaaga_2{ margin-left:1em; } div.pe_shiram{ font-stle:bold; min-width:7em; padding:0.3em; font-size:1.5em; border:1px solid black; min-width:7em; } span.pe_pradhaanapada{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold text-decoration:underline; color:black; } span.pe_vibhaaganaama_1{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; color:#133b5a; } span.pe_vibhaagasaMkhya_1{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; color:#133b5a; } a.pe_a_pglink{ text-decoration:none; color:blue; } a.pe_a_pada:link,a.pe_a_pada:visited,a.pe_a_pada{ text-decoration:none; color:#1A163A; } a.pe_a_pada_v:link,a.pe_a_pada_v:visited{ text-decoration:none; color:inherit; } a.pe_a_pada:hover{ text-decoration: underline; color:#1A163A; } a.pe_a_pada_v:hover{ text-decoration: underline; } div.pe_shir_shira{ max-width:15em; text-align:left; float:left; margin:0; }  div.pe_shiraputa{ max-width:15em; text-align:right; float:right; } div.pe_vivarana{ text-align:justify; } blockquote.pe_padyam{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; font-size:1.7em; } table.pe_cnpaTTika{ margin-left:2em; } </style><br><div class="pe_tera"><div class="pe_patra"><div class="pe_shir_shira"><div class="pe_shiram">सरस्वत्यर्णुआसंगम</div></div><div class="pe_shiraputa"><a class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_@6300">«</a>word5<a class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_@6302">»</a><br><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn696L">↶</a><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn696R">P696R</a><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn697L">↷</a></div><div class="floatclr" style="clear:both;"><hr><br></div><div class="pe_vivarana"><span class="pe_pradhaanapada">SARASVATYARṆUĀSAṄGAMA</span>  . A sacred place in <a class="pe_a_pada" href="कुरुक्षेत्र">kurukṣetra</a>. One who bathes here and fasts for <a class="pe_a_pada" href="थ्रेए">three</a> nights will be freed from the sin of <a class="pe_a_pada" href="ब्रह्महत्या">brahmahatyā</a> (killing of a brahmin). (Vana Parva, Chapter 83).</div></div></div>

शरवण|శరవణ|ಶರವಣ|śaravaṇa|sharavaNa|_pe_@6302|_pe_pn696R
