āmā</a>, the other nine being <a class="pe_a_pada" href="भानु">bhānu</a>, <a class="pe_a_pada" href="स्वर्भानु">svarbhānu</a>, <a class="pe_a_pada" href="प्रभानु">prabhānu</a>, <a class="pe_a_pada" href="भानुमान्">bhānumān</a>, Candrabhānu, <a class="pe_a_pada" href="बृहद्भानु">bṛhadbhānu</a>, Havirbhānu, <a class="pe_a_pada" href="श्रीभानु">śrībhānu</a> and <a class="pe_a_pada" href="प्रतिभानु">pratibhānu</a>. (<a class="pe_a_pada" href="भागवत">bhāgavata</a>, 10th <a class="pe_a_pada" href="स्कन्ध">skandha</a>).</div></div></div>

