<style>div.pe_tera{ font-family:Verdana, "Lucida Sans Unicode", sans-serif; margin: 0 auto 0 auto; line-height:1.5em; color:black; } div.pe_patra{ margin:0 auto 0 auto; padding: 1em; max-width:55.8em; font-size: 1em; } div.pe_vibhaaga_1{ margin-top:0.5em; } p.pe_vibhaaga_2{ margin-left:1em; } div.pe_shiram{ font-stle:bold; min-width:7em; padding:0.3em; font-size:1.5em; border:1px solid black; min-width:7em; } span.pe_pradhaanapada{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold text-decoration:underline; color:black; } span.pe_vibhaaganaama_1{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; color:#133b5a; } span.pe_vibhaagasaMkhya_1{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; color:#133b5a; } a.pe_a_pglink{ text-decoration:none; color:blue; } a.pe_a_pada:link,a.pe_a_pada:visited,a.pe_a_pada{ text-decoration:none; color:#1A163A; } a.pe_a_pada_v:link,a.pe_a_pada_v:visited{ text-decoration:none; color:inherit; } a.pe_a_pada:hover{ text-decoration: underline; color:#1A163A; } a.pe_a_pada_v:hover{ text-decoration: underline; } div.pe_shir_shira{ max-width:15em; text-align:left; float:left; margin:0; }  div.pe_shiraputa{ max-width:15em; text-align:right; float:right; } div.pe_vivarana{ text-align:justify; } blockquote.pe_padyam{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; font-size:1.7em; } table.pe_cnpaTTika{ margin-left:2em; } </style><br><div class="pe_tera"><div class="pe_patra"><div class="pe_shir_shira"><div class="pe_shiram">सुधनुस् १</div></div><div class="pe_shiraputa"><a class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_@6946">«</a>word4<a class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_@6948">»</a><br><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn753L">↶</a><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn754R">P754R</a><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn755L">↷</a></div><div class="floatclr" style="clear:both;"><hr><br></div><div class="pe_vivarana"><span class="pe_pradhaanapada">SUDHANUS I</span>  . A King of the <a class="pe_a_pada" href="पुरु">puru</a> dynasty. He was the son of King <a class="pe_a_pada" href="कुरु">kuru</a> who had founded <a class="pe_a_pada" href="कुरुक्षेत्र">kurukṣetra</a>. Four sons named <a class="pe_a_pada" href="सुधन्वा">sudhanvā</a>, <a class="pe_a_pada" href="सुधनुस्">sudhanus</a>, <a class="pe_a_pada" href="परीक्षित्">parīkṣit</a> and <a class="pe_a_pada" href="अरिमेजय">arimejaya</a>, were born to <a class="pe_a_pada" href="कुरु">kuru</a>. (<a class="pe_a_pada" href="अग्नि">agni</a> <a class="pe_a_pada" href="पुराण">purāṇa</a>, Chapter 278).</div></div></div>

सुधनुस्_२|सुधनुस्|సుధనుస్_౨|సుధనుస్|ಸುಧನುಸ್_೨|ಸುಧನುಸ್|sudhanus_2|sudhanus|_pe_@6948|_pe_pn754R
<style>div.pe_tera{ font-family:Verdana, "Lucida Sans Unicode", sans-serif; margin: 0 auto 0 auto; line-height:1.5em; color:black; } div.pe_patra{ margin:0 auto 0 auto; padding: 1em; max-width:55.8em; font-size: 1em; } div.pe_vibhaaga_1{ margin-top:0.5em; } p.pe_vibhaaga_2{ margin-left:1em; } div.pe_shiram{ font-stle:bold; min-width:7em; padding:0.3em; font-size:1.5em; border:1px solid black; min-width:7em; } span.pe_pradhaanapada{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold text-decoration:underline; color:black; } span.pe_vibhaaganaama_1{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; color:#133b5a; } span.pe_vibhaagasaMkhya_1{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; color:#133b5a; } a.pe_a_pglink{ text-decoration:none; color:blue; } a.pe_a_pada:link,a.pe_a_pada:visited,a.pe_a_pada{ text-decoration:none; color:#1A163A; } a.pe_a_pada_v:link,a.pe_a_pada_v:visited{ text-decoration:none; color:inherit; } a.pe_a_pada:hover{ text-decoration: underline; color:#1A163A; } a.pe_a_pada_v:hover{ text-decoration: underline; } div.pe_shir_shira{ max-width:15em; text-align:left; float:left; margin:0; }  div.pe_shiraputa{ max-width:15em; text-align:right; float:right; } div.pe_vivarana{ text-align:justify; } blockquote.pe_padyam{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; font-size:1.7em; } table.pe_cnpaTTika{ margin-left:2em; } </style><br><div class="pe_tera"><div class="pe_patra"><div class="pe_shir_shira"><div class="pe_shiram">सुधनुस् २</div></div><div class="pe_shiraputa"><a class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_@6947">«</a>word5<a class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_@6949">»</a><br><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn753L">↶</a><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn754R">P754R</a><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn755L">↷</a></div><div class="floatclr" style="clear:both;"><hr><br></div><div class="pe_vivarana"><span class="pe_pradhaanapada">SUDHANUS II</span>  . A King who was the son of <a class="pe_a_pada" href="कुरु">kuru</a> and the father of <a class="pe_a_pada" href="सुहोत्र">suhotra</a>. The King <a class="pe_a_pada" href="उपरिचरवसु">uparicaravasu</a> was a King of this dynasty. (<a class="pe_a_pada" href="भागवत">bhāgavata</a>, <a class="pe_a_pada" href="स्कन्ध">skandha</a> 9).</div></div></div>

सुधनुस्_३|सुधनुस्|సుధనుస్_౩|సుధనుస్|ಸುಧನುಸ್_೩|ಸುಧನುಸ್|sudhanus_3|sudhanus|_pe_@6949|_pe_pn754R
<style>div.pe_tera{ font-family:Verdana, "Lucida Sans Unicode", sans-serif; margin: 0 auto 0 auto; line-height:1.5em; color:black; } div.pe_patra{ margin:0 auto 0 auto; padding: 1em; max-width:55.8em; font-size: 1em; } div.pe_vibhaaga_1{ margin-top:0.5em; } p.pe_vibhaaga_2{ margin-left:1em; } div.pe_shiram{ font-stle:bold; min-width:7em; padding:0.3em; font-size:1.5em; border:1px solid black; min-width:7em; } span.pe_pradhaanapada{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold text-decoration:underline; color:black; } span.pe_vibhaaganaama_1{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; color:#133b5a; } span.pe_vibhaagasaMkhya_1{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; color:#133b5a; } a.pe_a_pglink{ text-decoration:none; color:blue; } a.pe_a_pada:link,a.pe_a_pada:visited,a.pe_a_pada{ text-decoration:none; color:#1A163A; } a.pe_a_pada_v:link,a.pe_a_pada_v:visited{ text-decoration:none; color:inherit; } a.pe_a_pada:hover{ text-decoration: underline; color:#1A163A; } a.pe_a_pada_v:hover{ text-decoration: underline; } div.pe_shir_shira{ max-width:15em; text-align:left; float:left; margin:0; }  div.pe_shiraputa{ max-width:15em; text-align:right; float:right; } div.pe_vivarana{ text-align:justify; } blockquote.pe_padyam{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; font-size:1.7em; } table.pe_cnpaTTika{ margin-left:2em; } </style><br><div class="pe_tera"><div class="pe_patra"><div class="pe_shir_shira"><div class="pe_shiram">सुधनुस् ३</div></div><div class="pe_shiraputa"><a class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_@6948">«</a>word6<a class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_@6950">»</a><br><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn753L">↶</a><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn754R">P754R</a><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn755L">↷</a></div><div class="floatclr" style="clear:both;"><hr><br></div><div class="pe_vivarana"><span class="pe_pradhaanapada">SUDHANUS III</span>  . A warrior from <a class="pe_a_pada" href="पाञ्चाल">pāñcāla</a> who took the side of the <a class="pe_a_pada" href="पाण्डवस्">pāṇḍavas</a>. This mighty warrior was the son of King <a class="pe_a_pada" href="द्रुपद">drupada</a> and the brother of <a class="pe_a_pada" href="वीरकेतु">vīraketu</a>. In the battle of <a class="pe_a_pada" href="भारत">bhārata</a>, when <a class="pe_a_pada" href="वीरकेतु">vīraketu</a> was killed, <a class="pe_a_pada" href="सुधनुस्">sudhanus</a> gathered his brothers and attacked <a class="pe_a_pada" href="द्रोण">droṇa</a>. In that fight <a class="pe_a_pada" href="सुधनुस्">sudhanus</a> was killed by <a class="pe_a_pada" href="द्रोण">droṇa</a>. (M.B. <a class="pe_a_pada" href="द्रोण पर्व">droṇa parva</a>, Chapter 98, Verses 37-40).</div></div></div>

सुधन्वा_१|सुधन्वा|సుధన్వా_౧|సుధన్వా|ಸುಧನ್ವಾ_೧|ಸುಧನ್ವಾ|sudhanvā_1|sudhanvā|sudhanvaa_1|sudhanvaa|_pe_@6950|_pe_pn754R
<style>div.pe_tera{ font-family:Verdana, "Lucida Sans Unicode", sans-serif; margin: 0 auto 0 auto; line-height:1.5em; color:black; } div.pe_patra{ margin:0 auto 0 auto; padding: 1em; max-width:55.8em; font-size: 1em; } div.pe_vibhaaga_1{ margin-top:0.5em; } p.pe_vibhaaga_2{ margin-left:1em; } div.pe_shiram{ font-stle:bold; min-width:7em; padding:0.3em; font-size:1.5em; border:1px solid black; min-width:7em; } span.pe_pradhaanapada{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold text-decoration:underline; color:black; } span.pe_vibhaaganaama_1{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; color:#133b5a; } span.pe_vibhaagasaMkhya_1{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; color:#133b5a; } a.pe_a_pglink{ text-decoration:none; color:blue; } a.pe_a_pada:link,a.pe_a_pada:visited,a.pe_a_pada{ text-decoration:none; color:#1A163A; } a.pe_a_pada_v:link,a.pe_a_pada_v:visited{ text-decoration:none; color:inherit; } a.pe_a_pada:hover{ text-decoration: underline; color:#1A163A; } a.pe_a_pada_v:hover{ text-decoration: underline; } div.pe_shir_shira{ max-width:15em; text-align:left; float:left; margin:0; }  div.pe_shiraputa{ max-width:15em; text-align:right; float:right; } div.pe_vivarana{ text-align:justify; } blockquote.pe_padyam{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; font-size:1.7em; } table.pe_cnpaTTika{ margin-left:2em; } </style><br><div class="pe_tera"><div class="pe_patra"><div class="pe_shir_shira"><div class="pe_shiram">सुधन्वा १</div></div><div class="pe_shiraputa"><a class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_@6949">«</a>word7<a class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_@6951">»</a><br><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn753L">↶</a><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn754R">P754R</a><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn755L">↷</a></div><div class="floatclr" style="clear:both;"><hr><br></div><div class="pe_vivarana"><span class="pe_pradhaanapada">SUDHANVĀ I</span>  . A guard of the ends of the quarters. In the beginning of <a class="pe_a_pada" href="च्रेअतिओन्">creation</a> <a class="pe_a_pada" href="ब्रह्मा">brahmā</a> made four guards of the four ends. They were <a class="pe_a_pada" href="सुधन्वा">sudhanvā</a> in the East, Śaṅkhapāda in the South, <a class="pe_a_pada" href="केतुमान्">ketumān</a> in the West and Hiraṇyaromā in the North. (<a class="pe_a_pada" href="अग्नि">agni</a> <a class="pe_a_pada" href="पुराण">purāṇa</a>, Chapter 19).</div></div></div>

सुधन्वा_२|सुधन्वा|సుధన్వా_౨|సుధన్వా|ಸುಧನ್ವಾ_೨|ಸುಧನ್ವಾ|sudhanvā_2|sudhanvā|sudhanvaa_2|sudhanvaa|_pe_@6951|_pe_pn754R
<style>div.pe_tera{ font-family:Verdana, "Lucida Sans Unicode", sans-serif; margin: 0 auto 0 auto; line-height:1.5em; color:black; } div.pe_patra{ margin:0 auto 0 auto; padding: 1em; max-width:55.8em; font-size: 1em; } div.pe_vibhaaga_1{ margin-top:0.5em; } p.pe_vibhaaga_2{ margin-left:1em; } div.pe_shiram{ font-stle:bold; min-width:7em; padding:0.3em; font-size:1.5em; border:1px solid black; min-width:7em; } span.pe_pradhaanapada{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold text-decoration:underline; color:black; } span.pe_vibhaaganaama_1{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; color:#133b5a; } span.pe_vibhaagasaMkhya_1{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; color:#133b5a; } a.pe_a_pglink{ text-decoration:none; color:blue; } a.pe_a_pada:link,a.pe_a_pada:visited,a.pe_a_pada{ text-decoration:none; color:#1A163A; } a.pe_a_pada_v:link,a.pe_a_pada_v:visited{ text-decoration:none; color:inherit; } a.pe_a_pada:hover{ text-decoration: underline; color:#1A163A; } a.pe_a_pada_v:hover{ text-decoration: underline; } div.pe_shir_shira{ max-width:15em; text-align:left; float:left; margin:0; }  div.pe_shiraputa{ max-width:15em; text-align:right; float:right; } div.pe_vivarana{ text-align:justify; } blockquote.pe_padyam{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; font-size:1.7em; } table.pe_cnpaTTika{ margin-left:2em; } </style><br><div class="pe_tera"><div class="pe_patra"><div class="pe_shir_shira"><div class="pe_shiram">सुधन्वा २</div></div><div class="pe_shiraputa"><a class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_@6950">«</a>word8<a class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_@6952">»</a><br><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn753L">↶</a><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn754R">P754R</a><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn755L">↷</a></div><div class="floatclr" style="clear:both;"><hr><br></div><div class="pe_vivarana"><span class="pe_pradhaanapada">SUDHANVĀ II</span>  . Son of hermit <a class="pe_a_pada" href="अंगिरस्">aṅgiras</a>. Some information gathered from <a class="pe_a_pada" href="ऋग्वेद">ṛgveda</a> and <a class="pe_a_pada" href="महाभारत">mahābhārata</a> is given below.</p><p class="pe_vibhaaga_2"><span class="vibhaagasaMkhya_2">(i) </span> There arose a contest between <a class="pe_a_pada" href="सुधन्वा">sudhanvā</a> and <a class="pe_a_pada" href="विरोचन">virocana</a>, the son of <a class="pe_a_pada" href="प्रह्लाद">prahlāda</a> for marrying the damsel <a class="pe_a_pada" href="केशिनी">keśinī</a>. (For detailed story see under <a class="pe_a_pada" href="केशिनी">keśinī</a> V).</p><p class="pe_vibhaaga_2"><span class="vibhaagasaMkhya_2">(ii) </span> This hermit visited <a class="pe_a_pada" href="भीष्म">bhīṣma</a> in his bed of arrows.<span class="NIvirupu"><br><br></span>(M.B. <a class="pe_a_pada" href="अनुशासन पर्व">anuśāsana parva</a>, Chapter 26, Verse 7).</p><p class="pe_vibhaaga_2"><span class="vibhaagasaMkhya_2">(iii) </span> <a class="pe_a_pada" href="सुधन्वा">sudhanvā</a> was the eighth son of <a class="pe_a_pada" href="अंगिरस्">aṅgiras</a>. </p><p class="pe_vibhaaga_2"><span class="vibhaagasaMkhya_2">(iv) </span> It is stated in <a class="pe_a_pada" href="महाभारत">mahābhārata</a>, <a class="pe_a_pada" href="अनुशासन पर्व">anuśāsana parva</a>, Chapter 86, Verse 24, that this <a class="pe_a_pada" href="सुधन्वा">sudhanvā</a> gave <a class="pe_a_pada" href="सुब्रह्मण्य">subrahmaṇya</a> a chariot, in the battle between the <a class="pe_a_pada" href="देवस्">devas</a> and the asuras.</p><p class="pe_vibhaaga_2"><span class="vibhaagasaMkhya_2">(v) </span> <a class="pe_a_pada" href="सुधन्वा">sudhanvā</a> had <a class="pe_a_pada" href="थ्रेए">three</a> sons called <a class="pe_a_pada" href="ऋभु">ṛbhu</a>, <a class="pe_a_pada" href="विभ्वा">vibhvā</a> and <a class="pe_a_pada" href="वाज">vāja</a>. (<a class="pe_a_pada" href="ऋग्वेद">ṛgveda</a>, Maṇḍala 1, Anuvāka 16, Sūkta 111).</div></div></div>

सुधन्वा_३|सुधन्वा|సుధన్వా_౩|సుధన్వా|ಸುಧನ್ವಾ_೩|ಸುಧನ್ವಾ|sudhanvā_3|sudhanvā|sudhanvaa_3|sudhanvaa|_pe_@6952|_pe_pn755L
<style>div.pe_tera{ font-family:Verdana, "Lucida Sans Unicode", sans-serif; margin: 0 auto 0 auto; line-height:1.5em; color:black; } div.pe_patra{ margin:0 auto 0 auto; padding: 1em; max-width:55.8em; font-size: 1em; } div.pe_vibhaaga_1{ margin-top:0.5em; } p.pe_vibhaaga_2{ margin-left:1em; } div.pe_shiram{ font-stle:bold; min-width:7em; padding:0.3em; font-size:1.5em; border:1px solid black; min-width:7em; } span.pe_pradhaanapada{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold text-decoration:underline; color:black; } span.pe_vibhaaganaama_1{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; color:#133b5a; } span.pe_vibhaagasaMkhya_1{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; color:#133b5a; } a.pe_a_pglink{ text-decoration:none; color:blue; } a.pe_a_pada:link,a.pe_a_pada:visited,a.pe_a_pada{ text-decoration:none; color:#1A163A; } a.pe_a_pada_v:link,a.pe_a_pada_v:visited{ text-decoration:none; color:inherit; } a.pe_a_pada:hover{ text-decoration: underline; color:#1A163A; } a.pe_a_pada_v:hover{ text-decoration: underline; } div.pe_shir_shira{ max-width:15em; text-align:left; float:left; margin:0; }  div.pe_shiraputa{ max-width:15em; text-align:right; float:right; } div.pe_vivarana{ text-align:justify; } blockquote.pe_padyam{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; font-size:1.7em; } table.pe_cnpaTTika{ margin-left:2em; } </style><br><div class="pe_tera"><div class="pe_patra"><div class="pe_shir_shira"><div class="pe_shiram">सुधन्वा ३</div></div><div class="pe_shiraputa"><a class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_@6951">«</a>word1<a class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_@6953">»</a><br><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn754R">↶</a><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn755L">P755L</a><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn755R">↷</a></div><div class="floatclr" style="clear:both;"><hr><br></div><div class="pe_vivarana"><span class="pe_pradhaanapada">SUDHANVĀ III</span>  . A great warrior who fought against the <a class="pe_a_pada" href="पाण्डवस्">pāṇḍavas</a> in the battle of <a class="pe_a_pada" href="कुरुक्षेत्र">kurukṣetra</a>. He was killed by <a class="pe_a_pada" href="अर्जुन">arjuna</a>. (M.B. <a class="pe_a_pada" href="द्रोण पर्व">droṇa parva</a>, Chapter 18, Verse 42).</div></div></div>

सुधन्वा_४|सुधन्वा|సుధన్వా_౪|సుధన్వా|ಸುಧನ್ವಾ_೪|ಸುಧನ್ವಾ|sudhanvā_4|sudhanvā|sudhanvaa_4|sudhanvaa|_pe_@6953|_pe_pn755L
<style>div.pe_tera{ font-family:Verdana, "Lucida Sans Unicode", sans-serif; margin: 0 auto 0 auto; line-height:1.5em; color:black; } div.pe_patra{ margin:0 auto 0 auto; padding: 1em; max-width:55.8em; font-size: 1em; } div.pe_vibhaaga_1{ margin-top:0.5em; } p.pe_vibhaaga_2{ margin-left:1em; } div.pe_shiram{ font-stle:bold; min-width:7em; padding:0.3em; font-size:1.5em; border:1px solid black; min-width:7em; } span.pe_pradhaanapada{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold text-decoration:underline; color:black; } span.pe_vibhaaganaama_1{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; color:#133b5a; } span.pe_vibhaagasaMkhya_1{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; color:#133b5a; } a.pe_a_pglink{ text-decoration:none; color:blue; } a.pe_a_pada:link,a.pe_a_pada:visited,a.pe_a_pada{ text-decoration:none; color:#1A163A; } a.pe_a_pada_v:link,a.pe_a_pada_v:visited{ text-decoration:none; color:inherit; } a.pe_a_pada:hover{ text-decoration: underline; color:#1A163A; } a.pe_a_pada_v:hover{ text-decoration: underline; } div.pe_shir_shira{ max-width:15em; text-align:left; float:left; margin:0; }  div.pe_shiraputa{ max-width:15em; text-align:right; float:right; } div.pe_vivarana{ text-align:justify; } blockquote.pe_padyam{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; font-size:1.7em; } table.pe_cnpaTTika{ margin-left:2em; } </style><br><div class="pe_tera"><div class="pe_patra"><div class="pe_shir_shira"><div class="pe_shiram">सुधन्वा ४</div></div><div class="pe_shiraputa"><a class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_@6952">«</a>word2<a class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_@6954">»</a><br><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn754R">↶</a><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn755L">P755L</a><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn755R">↷</a></div><div class="floatclr" style="clear:both;"><hr><br></div><div class="pe_vivarana"><span class="pe_pradhaanapada">SUDHANVĀ IV</span>  . A <a class="pe_a_pada" href="सुधन्वा">sudhanvā</a> who was the son of <a class="pe_a_pada" href="द्रुपद">drupada</a>, is mentioned in <a class="pe_a_pada" href="महाभारत">mahābhārata</a>, <a class="pe_a_pada" href="द्रोण पर्व">droṇa parva</a>, Chapter 23, Verse 44. This warrior sided with the <a class="pe_a_pada" href="पाण्डवस्">pāṇḍavas</a> in the battle of <a class="pe_a_pada" href="कुरुक्षेत्र">kurukṣetra</a> and fought against the <a class="pe_a_pada" href="कौरवस्">kauravas</a>. When his brother <a class="pe_a_pada" href="वीरकेतु">vīraketu</a> was killed, he and his brothers joined together and attacked <a class="pe_a_pada" href="द्रोण">droṇa</a>. In that fight <a class="pe_a_pada" href="द्रोण">droṇa</a> killed <a class="pe_a_pada" href="सुधन्वा">sudhanvā</a>. (M.B. <a class="pe_a_pada" href="द्रोण पर्व">droṇa parva</a>, Chapter 122, Verse 45).</div></div></div>

सुधन्वा_५|सुधन्वा|సుధన్వా_౫|సుధన్వా|ಸುಧನ್ವಾ_೫|ಸುಧನ್ವಾ|sudhanvā_5|sudhanvā|sudhanvaa_5|sudhanvaa|_pe_@6954|_pe_pn755L
<style>div.pe_tera{ font-family:Verdana, "Lucida Sans Unicode", sans-serif; margin: 0 auto 0 auto; line-height:1.5em; color:black; } div.pe_patra{ margin:0 auto 0 auto; padding: 1em; max-width:55.8em; font-size: 1em; } div.pe_vibhaaga_1{ margin-top:0.5em; } p.pe_vibhaaga_2{ margin-left:1em; } div.pe_shiram{ font-stle:bold; min-width:7em; padding:0.3em; font-size:1.5em; border:1px solid black; min-width:7em; } span.pe_pradhaanapada{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold text-decoration:underline; color:black; } span.pe_vibhaaganaama_1{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; color:#133b5a; } span.pe_vibhaagasaMkhya_1{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; color:#133b5a; } a.pe_a_pglink{ text-decoration:none; color:blue; } a.pe_a_pada:link,a.pe_a_pada:visited,a.pe_a_pada{ text-decoration:none; color:#1A163A; } a.pe_a_pada_v:link,a.pe_a_pada_v:visited{ text-decoration:none; color:inherit; } a.pe_a_pada:hover{ text-decoration: underline; color:#1A163A; } a.pe_a_pada_v:hover{ text-decoration: underline; } div.pe_shir_shira{ max-width:15em; text-align:left; float:left; margin:0; }  div.pe_shiraputa{ max-width:15em; text-align:right; float:right; } div.pe_vivarana{ text-align:justify; } blockquote.pe_padyam{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; font-size:1.7em; } table.pe_cnpaTTika{ margin-left:2em; } </style><br><div class="pe_tera"><div class="pe_patra"><div class="pe_shir_shira"><div class="pe_shiram">सुधन्वा ५</div></div><div class="pe_shiraputa"><a class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_@6953">«</a>word3<a class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_@6955">»</a><br><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn754R">↶</a><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn755L">P755L</a><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn755R">↷</a></div><div class="floatclr" style="clear:both;"><hr><br></div><div class="pe_vivarana"><span class="pe_pradhaanapada">SUDHANVĀ V</span>  . An ancient King of <a class="pe_a_pada" href="भारत">bhārata</a>. A story that King <a class="pe_a_pada" href="मान्धाता">māndhātā</a> defeated this <a class="pe_a_pada" href="सुधन्वा">sudhanvā</a> in battle, occurs in Mahā <a class="pe_a_pada" href="भारत">bhārata</a>, <a class="pe_a_pada" href="द्रोण पर्व">droṇa parva</a>, Chapter 62</div></div></div>

सुधन्वा_६|सुधन्वा|సుధన్వా_౬|సుధన్వా|ಸುಧನ್ವಾ_೬|ಸುಧನ್ವಾ|sudhanvā_6|sudhanvā|sudhanvaa_6|sudhanvaa|_pe_@6955|_pe_pn755L
<style>div.pe_tera{ font-family:Verdana, "Lucida Sans Unicode", sans-serif; margin: 0 auto 0 auto; line-height:1.5em; color:black; } div.pe_patra{ margin:0 auto 0 auto; padding: 1em; max-width:55.8em; font-size: 1em; } div.pe_vibhaaga_1{ margin-top:0.5em; } p.pe_vibhaaga_2{ margin-left:1em; } div.pe_shiram{ font-stle:bold; min-width:7em; padding:0.3em; font-size:1.5em; border:1px solid black; min-width:7em; } span.pe_pradhaanapada{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold text-decoration:underline; color:black; } span.pe_vibhaaganaama_1{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; color:#133b5a; } span.pe_vibhaagasaMkhya_1{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; color:#133b5a; } a.pe_a_pglink{ text-decoration:none; color:blue; } a.pe_a_pada:link,a.pe_a_pada:visited,a.pe_a_pada{ text-decoration:none; color:#1A163A; } a.pe_a_pada_v:link,a.pe_a_pada_v:visited{ text-decoration:none; color:inherit; } a.pe_a_pada:hover{ text-decoration: underline; color:#1A163A; } a.pe_a_pada_v:hover{ text-decoration: underline; } div.pe_shir_shira{ max-width:15em; text-align:left; float:left; margin:0; }  div.pe_shiraputa{ max-width:15em; text-align:right; float:right; } div.pe_vivarana{ text-align:justify; } blockquote.pe_padyam{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; font-size:1.7em; } table.pe_cnpaTTika{ margin-left:2em; } </style><br><div class="pe_tera"><div class="pe_patra"><div class="pe_shir_shira"><div class="pe_shiram">सुधन्वा ६</div></div><div class="pe_shiraputa"><a class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_@6954">«</a>word4<a class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_@6956">»</a><br><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn754R">↶</a><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn755L">P755L</a><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn755R">↷</a></div><div class="floatclr" style="clear:both;"><hr><br></div><div class="pe_vivarana"><span class="pe_pradhaanapada">SUDHANVĀ VI</span>  . A King of <a class="pe_a_pada" href="सांकाश्य">sāṅkāśya</a>. This King surrounded the city of <a class="pe_a_pada" href="मिथिला">mithilā</a> and sent word that unless the bow of <a class="pe_a_pada" href="शिव">śiva</a> and the princess <a class="pe_a_pada" href="सीता">sītā</a> were given to him he would kill <a class="pe_a_pada" href="जनक">janaka</a>, who subsequently fought a battle with him. In this battle <a class="pe_a_pada" href="सुधन्वा">sudhanvā</a> was killed. <a class="pe_a_pada" href="सांकाश्य">sāṅkāśya</a>, the kingdom of <a class="pe_a_pada" href="सुधन्वा">sudhanvā</a> was given to <a class="pe_a_pada" href="कुशध्वज">kuśadhvaja</a> by his brother <a class="pe_a_pada" href="जनक">janaka</a>. (<a class="pe_a_pada" href="वाल्मीकि">vālmīki</a> <a class="pe_a_pada" href="रामायण">rāmāyaṇa</a>, Bāla Kāṇḍa, <a class="pe_a_pada" href="सर्ग">sarga</a> 71).</div></div></div>

सुधर्मा_१|सुधर्मा|సుధర్మా_౧|సుధర్మా|ಸುಧರ್ಮಾ_೧|ಸುಧರ್ಮಾ|sudharmā_1|sudharmā|sudharmaa_1|sudharmaa|_pe_@6956|_pe_pn755L
