pada" href="भागवत">bhāgavata</a>, <a class="pe_a_pada" href="स्कन्ध">skandha</a> 10).</div></div></div>

सुधर्मा_२|सुधर्मा|సుధర్మా_౨|సుధర్మా|ಸುಧರ್ಮಾ_೨|ಸುಧರ್ಮಾ|sudharmā_2|sudharmā|sudharmaa_2|sudharmaa|_pe_@6957|_pe_pn755L
<style>div.pe_tera{ font-family:Verdana, "Lucida Sans Unicode", sans-serif; margin: 0 auto 0 auto; line-height:1.5em; color:black; } div.pe_patra{ margin:0 auto 0 auto; padding: 1em; max-width:55.8em; font-size: 1em; } div.pe_vibhaaga_1{ margin-top:0.5em; } p.pe_vibhaaga_2{ margin-left:1em; } div.pe_shiram{ font-stle:bold; min-width:7em; padding:0.3em; font-size:1.5em; border:1px solid black; min-width:7em; } span.pe_pradhaanapada{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold text-decoration:underline; color:black; } span.pe_vibhaaganaama_1{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; color:#133b5a; } span.pe_vibhaagasaMkhya_1{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; color:#133b5a; } a.pe_a_pglink{ text-decoration:none; color:blue; } a.pe_a_pada:link,a.pe_a_pada:visited,a.pe_a_pada{ text-decoration:none; color:#1A163A; } a.pe_a_pada_v:link,a.pe_a_pada_v:visited{ text-decoration:none; color:inherit; } a.pe_a_pada:hover{ text-decoration: underline; color:#1A163A; } a.pe_a_pada_v:hover{ text-decoration: underline; } div.pe_shir_shira{ max-width:15em; text-align:left; float:left; margin:0; }  div.pe_shiraputa{ max-width:15em; text-align:right; float:right; } div.pe_vivarana{ text-align:justify; } blockquote.pe_padyam{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; font-size:1.7em; } table.pe_cnpaTTika{ margin-left:2em; } </style><br><div class="pe_tera"><div class="pe_patra"><div class="pe_shir_shira"><div class="pe_shiram">सुधर्मा २</div></div><div class="pe_shiraputa"><a class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_@6956">«</a>word6<a class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_@6958">»</a><br><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn754R">↶</a><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn755L">P755L</a><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn755R">↷</a></div><div class="floatclr" style="clear:both;"><hr><br></div><div class="pe_vivarana"><span class="pe_pradhaanapada">SUDHARMĀ II</span>  . The great assembly hall of the Yādavas. It is mentioned in <a class="pe_a_pada" href="महाभारत">mahābhārata</a>, Ādi Parva, Chapter 219, Verse 10, that at the time of the carrying away of <a class="pe_a_pada" href="सुभद्रा">subhadrā</a>, the soldiers ran to <a class="pe_a_pada" href="सुधर्मा">sudharmā</a> and reported the matter there. This hall had the name ‘Dāśārhī’ also. This great hall was one yojana long and one yojana broad. It was in this hall that Śrī <a class="pe_a_pada" href="कृष्ण">kṛṣṇa</a> received <a class="pe_a_pada" href="इन्द्र">indra</a>. (M.B. Dākṣiṇātya Pāṭha, Sabhā Parva, Chapter 38).</div></div></div>

सुधर्मा_३|सुधर्मा|సుధర్మా_౩|సుధర్మా|ಸುಧರ್ಮಾ_೩|ಸುಧರ್ಮಾ|sudharmā_3|sudharmā|sudharmaa_3|sudharmaa|_pe_@6958|_pe_pn755L
<style>div.pe_tera{ font-family:Verdana, "Lucida Sans Unicode", sans-serif; margin: 0 auto 0 auto; line-height:1.5em; color:black; } div.pe_patra{ margin:0 auto 0 auto; padding: 1em; max-width:55.8em; font-size: 1em; } div.pe_vibhaaga_1{ margin-top:0.5em; } p.pe_vibhaaga_2{ margin-left:1em; } div.pe_shiram{ font-stle:bold; min-width:7em; padding:0.3em; font-size:1.5em; border:1px solid black; min-width:7em; } span.pe_pradhaanapada{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold text-decoration:underline; color:black; } span.pe_vibhaaganaama_1{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; color:#133b5a; } span.pe_vibhaagasaMkhya_1{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; color:#133b5a; } a.pe_a_pglink{ text-decoration:none; color:blue; } a.pe_a_pada:link,a.pe_a_pada:visited,a.pe_a_pada{ text-decoration:none; color:#1A163A; } a.pe_a_pada_v:link,a.pe_a_pada_v:visited{ text-decoration:none; color:inherit; } a.pe_a_pada:hover{ text-decoration: underline; color:#1A163A; } a.pe_a_pada_v:hover{ text-decoration: underline; } div.pe_shir_shira{ max-width:15em; text-align:left; float:left; margin:0; }  div.pe_shiraputa{ max-width:15em; text-align:right; float:right; } div.pe_vivarana{ text-align:justify; } blockquote.pe_padyam{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; font-size:1.7em; } table.pe_cnpaTTika{ margin-left:2em; } </style><br><div class="pe_tera"><div class="pe_patra"><div class="pe_shir_shira"><div class="pe_shiram">सुधर्मा ३</div></div><div class="pe_shiraputa"><a class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_@6957">«</a>word7<a class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_@6959">»</a><br><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn754R">↶</a><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn755L">P755L</a><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn755R">↷</a></div><div class="floatclr" style="clear:both;"><hr><br></div><div class="pe_vivarana"><span class="pe_pradhaanapada">SUDHARMĀ III</span>  . Wife of <a class="pe_a_pada" href="मातलि">mātali</a>, who was the charioteer of <a class="pe_a_pada" href="इन्द्र">indra</a>. It is mentioned in the <a class="pe_a_pada" href="महाभारत">mahābhārata</a>, Udyoga Parva, Chapter 95, that a daughter named <a class="pe_a_pada" href="गुणकेशी">guṇakeśī</a> was born to <a class="pe_a_pada" href="मातलि">mātali</a> by <a class="pe_a_pada" href="सुधर्मा">sudharmā</a>.</div></div></div>

सुधर्मा_४|सुधर्मा|సుధర్మా_౪|సుధర్మా|ಸುಧರ್ಮಾ_೪|ಸುಧರ್ಮಾ|sudharmā_4|sudharmā|sudharmaa_4|sudharmaa|_pe_@6959|_pe_pn755L
<style>div.pe_tera{ font-family:Verdana, "Lucida Sans Unicode", sans-serif; margin: 0 auto 0 auto; line-height:1.5em; color:black; } div.pe_patra{ margin:0 auto 0 auto; padding: 1em; max-width:55.8em; font-size: 1em; } div.pe_vibhaaga_1{ margin-top:0.5em; } p.pe_vibhaaga_2{ margin-left:1em; } div.pe_shiram{ font-stle:bold; min-width:7em; padding:0.3em; font-size:1.5em; border:1px solid black; min-width:7em; } span.pe_pradhaanapada{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold text-decoration:underline; color:black; } span.pe_vibhaaganaama_1{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; color:#133b5a; } span.pe_vibhaagasaMkhya_1{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; color:#133b5a; } a.pe_a_pglink{ text-decoration:none; color:blue; } a.pe_a_pada:link,a.pe_a_pada:visited,a.pe_a_pada{ text-decoration:none; color:#1A163A; } a.pe_a_pada_v:link,a.pe_a_pada_v:visited{ text-decoration:none; color:inherit; } a.pe_a_pada:hover{ text-decoration: underline; color:#1A163A; } a.pe_a_pada_v:hover{ text-decoration: underline; } div.pe_shir_shira{ max-width:15em; text-align:left; float:left; margin:0; }  div.pe_shiraputa{ max-width:15em; text-align:right; float:right; } div.pe_vivarana{ text-align:justify; } blockquote.pe_padyam{ font-style:italic; font-weight:bold; font-size:1.7em; } table.pe_cnpaTTika{ margin-left:2em; } </style><br><div class="pe_tera"><div class="pe_patra"><div class="pe_shir_shira"><div class="pe_shiram">सुधर्मा ४</div></div><div class="pe_shiraputa"><a class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_@6958">«</a>word8<a class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_@6960">»</a><br><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn754R">↶</a><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn755L">P755L</a><a class="pe_a_pglink" class="pe_a_pglink" href="_pe_pn755R">↷</a></div><div class="floatclr" style="clear:both;"><hr><br></div><div class="pe_vivarana"><span class="pe_pradhaanapada">SUDHARMĀ IV</span>  . A prince of the <a class="pe_a_pada" href="वृष्णि">vṛṣṇi</a> dynasty. It is stated in Mahā <a class="pe_a_pada" href="भारत">bhārata</a>, Sabhā Parva, Chapter 4, Verse 18, that he was a member of the assembly of <a class="pe_a_pada" href="युधिष्ठिर">yudhiṣṭhira</a> and that he had learned archery from <a class="pe_a_pada" href="अर्जुन">arjuna</a>.</div></div></div>

सुधर्मा_५|सुधर्मा|సుధర్మా_౫|సుధర్మా|ಸುಧರ್ಮಾ_೫|ಸುಧರ್ಮಾ|sudharmā_5|sudharmā|sudharmaa_5|sudharmaa|_pe_@6960|_pe_pn755L
