asty. <a class="pe_a_pada" href="सुह्व">suhva</a> was the son of <a class="pe_a_pada" href="बलि">bali</a>, and grandson of <a class="pe_a_pada" href="सुतपस्">sutapas</a>. <a class="pe_a_pada" href="बलि">bali</a> had no direct sons. Being miserable due to the absence of sons, <a class="pe_a_pada" href="बलि">bali</a> approached the hermit <a class="pe_a_pada" href="दीर्घतमस्">dīrghatamas</a>, by whom the queen gave birth to six sons. They were <a class="pe_a_pada" href="अंग">aṅga</a>, Vanga, <a class="pe_a_pada" href="कलिंग">kaliṅga</a>, <a class="pe_a_pada" href="सुह्व">suhva</a> (or <a class="pe_a_pada" href="सुह्म">suhma</a>), <a class="pe_a_pada" href="पुण्ड्र">puṇḍra</a> and Adrūpa. (<a class="pe_a_pada" href="भागवत">bhāgavata</a>, <a class="pe_a_pada" href="स्कन्ध">skandha</a> 9).</div></div></div>

