ass="pe_a_pada" href="उशीनर">uśīnara</a> who begot of his wife Nṛgā the son called <a class="pe_a_pada" href="नृग">nṛga</a>, <a class="pe_a_pada" href="नर">nara</a> by his wife, <a class="pe_a_pada" href="नरा">narā</a>; <a class="pe_a_pada" href="कृमि">kṛmi</a> by the wife <a class="pe_a_pada" href="कृमी">kṛmī</a>; Daśa by the wife <a class="pe_a_pada" href="सुव्रता">suvratā</a> and <a class="pe_a_pada" href="शिबि">śibi</a> by his wife <a class="pe_a_pada" href="दृषद्वती">dṛṣadvatī</a>. (<a class="pe_a_pada" href="अग्नि">agni</a> <a class="pe_a_pada" href="पुराण">purāṇa</a>, Chapter 277).</div></div></div>

