 able to restore his dead son to  life. He did not eat meat. <a class="pe_a_pada" href="महाभारत">mahābhārata</a>, Anuśāsana Parva, Chapter 150 mentions that he was one of the few Kings who deserve to be remembered with reverence at dawn and dusk. (M.B. Ādi Parva, Chapter 1, Verse 233; <a class="pe_a_pada" href="शान्ति">śānti</a> Parva, Chapter 153, Verse 68; Anuśāsana Parva, Chapter 115, Verse 66).</div></div></div>

