following. <a class="pe_a_pada" href="श्री राम">śrī rāma</a>-<a class="pe_a_pada" href="कुश">kuśa</a>-AditiNiṣadha-Nabhas-<a class="pe_a_pada" href="पुण्डरीक">puṇḍarīka</a>-<a class="pe_a_pada" href="क्षेमधन्वा">kṣemadhanvā</a>-DevānīkaṚkṣa-<a class="pe_a_pada" href="पारियात्र">pāriyātra</a>-<a class="pe_a_pada" href="बल">bala</a>-<a class="pe_a_pada" href="विन्द">vinda</a>-<a class="pe_a_pada" href="वज्रनाभ">vajranābha</a>. <a class="pe_a_pada" href="खगण">khagaṇa</a> was the son of <a class="pe_a_pada" href="वज्रनाभ">vajranābha</a>. (<a class="pe_a_pada" href="भागवत">bhāgavata</a>, <a class="pe_a_pada" href="स्कन्ध">skandha</a> 9).</div></div></div>

