śyapa</a> of his wife <a class="pe_a_pada" href="दनु">danu</a>. It is mentioned in <a class="pe_a_pada" href="महाभारत">mahābhārata</a>, Ādi Parva Chapter 65, Stanza 25, that he was the most prominent of the <a class="pe_a_pada" href="तेन्">ten</a> sons of <a class="pe_a_pada" href="दनु">danu</a>.</div></div></div>

