स्">devas</a> and the Asuras churned the sea of Milk, four damsels were caused to arise by <a class="pe_a_pada" href="वरुण">varuṇa</a> and holy pot of Ambrosia, by <a class="pe_a_pada" href="सोम">soma</a>. The four damsels were <a class="pe_a_pada" href="सुलक्ष्मी">sulakṣmī</a>, <a class="pe_a_pada" href="वारुणी">vāruṇī</a>, <a class="pe_a_pada" href="कामोदा">kāmodā</a> and Śreṣṭhā, of whom <a class="pe_a_pada" href="वारुणी">vāruṇī</a> was married by <a class="pe_a_pada" href="देवस्">devas</a>. (<a class="pe_a_pada" href="पद्म">padma</a> <a class="pe_a_pada" href="पुराण">purāṇa</a>, <a class="pe_a_pada" href="भूमि">bhūmi</a> Khaṇḍa, Chapter 119).</div></div></div>

