href="महाभारत">mahābhārata</a>, Vana Parva, Chapter 221, Stanza 27, that if a woman during her monthly course happens to touch the holy fire, an aṣṭakapāla should be offered to the fire <a class="pe_a_pada" href="वसुमान्">vasumān</a>. This fire called <a class="pe_a_pada" href="वसुमान्">vasumān</a> now stays in the palace of <a class="pe_a_pada" href="ब्रह्मा">brahmā</a>. (M.B. Sabhā Parva, Chapter 11, stanza 30).</div></div></div>

